Z||000007||Rodrv6||10-29-2000||12:20 AM||||If you would rather "Buy American", there is a fellow in Illinois who is putting together an F-16 and an F-18 from parts.  Both aircraft are legal and will be for sale when they are complete.  Be the first on your block   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>You might be surprised at the number of old Soviet fighter airplanes that are in private hands here in the US.  Several years ago the Oshkosh airshow had 2 MIG 15's, 1 MIG 17, 1 MIG 21, an F-86 Sabre, and 2 F-104 Starfighters, all in private ownership.  What a show!!!<BR>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE<p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000008||Cheever2||10-29-2000||12:29 AM||||Hmmm.  F16 = 1 engine, 1 vertical stabilizer.<BR>       F18 = 2 engines, 2 vertical stabilizers.<P>I'd go for the F16.  Less to maintain, less to breakdown, less confusion to operate the control surfaces.  Besides, F18's were made primarily for carrier use, and that means MORE maintainance costs and less space for my Fieros.<P>||||reg||1
